<TrustPage title="Editorial team and review status | CalcsDesk" description="How CalcsDesk attributes its content and distinguishes automated source checks from human or qualified professional review." breadcrumb="Editorial team" eyebrow="Who checks the working" heading="Credit the work. Be clear about review." intro="CalcsDesk uses the byline “CalcsDesk Editorial Team” for its site content. That label does not mean a calculator has been reviewed by an accountant, tax adviser or other qualified professional.">
  <div class="trust-status-list"><div><strong>Current calculator betas</strong><p>Official-source check and automated calculation tests completed for the published beta scope.</p></div><div><strong>Human and professional review</strong><p>Pending. No qualified-reviewer credential or professional sign-off is claimed for these tools.</p></div></div>
  <h2>What the current checks cover.</h2><p>The 2026 federal beta uses rate records linked to official IRS and Social Security Administration publications. Its automated tests check published tax-schedule amounts, important bracket boundaries, deduction values, payroll-tax limits and invalid inputs.</p><p>Those checks can expose implementation mistakes. They cannot establish that every tax situation is covered, that the user chose the right filing status, or that a qualified person reviewed the content.</p>
  <p>The UK monthly-salary beta has HMRC rate and component-example checks; it is not a validated PAYE payslip. The UAE gratuity beta has a narrow source-checked accrual model, excludes cap-affected cases, and still needs official worked examples and cap clarification. The India salary comparison uses enacted current-year rules for a narrow resident-under-60 case; full official worked examples and human review remain pending. Each page states its own remaining checks. No review status carries automatically from one tool to another.</p><h2>What a review line will mean.</h2><p>If a qualified professional reviews a page in future, its review line will identify the professional’s role and the actual review date. A credential will be shown only when it is real and relevant to the work reviewed. A review of one calculator will not be applied to unrelated country pages or tools.</p><p>Until that work happens, review status must remain explicit. We do not add invented reviewer names, biographies, portraits or credentials.</p>
  <h2>AI assistance.</h2><p>AI tools have helped with the site’s structure, code, tests and draft explanations. The source references are external evidence; AI output itself is not an authority for a tax rate. Human verification is still part of the full-release requirements.</p>
  <h2>Read the evidence with the result.</h2><p>Use the <a href="/us/tax/income-tax-calculator/#rates-sources">federal beta’s rate tables and source links</a> to inspect its inputs. The <a href="/methodology/">methodology</a> describes the remaining release gates, and the <a href="/updates/">updates log</a> records published development changes.</p>
</TrustPage>
